,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-06-20T22:14:59Z","updated_at":"2026-06-21T02:11:06Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.6.3 and 4.7\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.stable - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 3 monitors - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9621) - 12th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-12600KF (16 threads) - 15.81 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using a texture with tiling as the grabber area for a VSlider and a HSlider, the visual behavior is distinctly different. The texture \"moves with\" the grabber on a VSlider, while it doesn't for a HSlider. Ideally, both should do the same thing or have a user-controlled setting to choose the fill behavior. See the attached video.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/905cddc1-df85-4811-9416-c1bb4620a993\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Setup a VSlider and HSlider\n2. In the theme, set the grabber_area_highlight and grabber_area StyleBoxes to a StyleBoxTexture w/ Axis Stretch set to \"Tile\"\n3. Observe the issue\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[SliderIssue.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/29167903/SliderIssue.zip)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120501/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":3},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120501/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}